(Abstract) Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
14 TL
(Mitochondrial dysfunction affects skeletal muscle \(SkM\) function and is critical in the) Tj T*
(etiology of age-related sarcopenia. The sirtuin 1-PGC1-alpha pathway is a key regulator of) Tj T*
(mitochondrial mass, structure, and function. However, pathway activity decreases with) Tj T*
(aging. Cacao flavanols show promise in their ability to activate mitochondrial pathways. We) Tj T*
(evaluated the capacity of the flavanol \(+\)-epicatechin \(+Epi\) to stimulate such a) Tj T*
(pathway and favorably impact mitochondrial and oxidative stress \(OS\)-associated endpoints) Tj T*
(in aged SkM. Using 23-month-old male Sprague-Dawley rats, an 8-week oral administration of) Tj T*
(+Epi \(1 mg/kg/day\) was implemented, and results were compared versus vehicle-treated) Tj T*
(controls. Assessments included the nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide \(NAD\)/sirtuin) Tj T*
(1/PGC1-alpha pathway, acetylated proteins levels, mitochondrial function and biogenesis, as) Tj T*
(well as OS-related endpoints in SkM. +Epi increased the NAD/NADH ratio, activation of) Tj T*
(sirtuin 1, the deacetylation of nuclear protein content, including that of PGC1-alpha.) Tj T*
(Also, +Epi induced increases of TFAM and NRF1 mRNA levels, deacetylation of mitochondrial) Tj T*
(complex I and V, increases in complex I activity, sirtuin 3, complexes I and V, mitofilin,) Tj T*
(and TFAM protein levels. SkM citrate synthase activity and ATP content increased with +Epi.) Tj T*
(OS markers in proteins and lipids were reduced, while buffering systems \(superoxide) Tj T*
(dismutase 2 and catalase protein and activities\) increased. In white blood cells, we) Tj T*
(documented serial reductions in mitochondrial DNA content and citrate synthase activity) Tj T*
(with aging, which were either fully or partially reversed with +Epi. Results demonstrate) Tj T*
(that +Epi treatment yields positive effects on mitochondrial biogenesis and function,) Tj T*
() Tj T*
